<title>CANADA: New Brunswick sets C$250 mln bond due June, 2017.</title>
<headline>New Brunswick sets C$250 mln bond due June, 2017.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Province of New Brunswick on Wednesday issued C$250 million of 6.75 percent bonds due June 27, 2017 in financial markets, said lead manager Nesbitt Burns.</p>
<p>The bond was priced at 99.339 to yield 6.811 percent, 20 basis points over the Government of Canada yield curve.</p>
<p>The bond will pay interest on December 27 and June 27 and will be delievered on June 27, 1997.</p>
<p>((Jeffrey Hodgson (416) 941-8105, e-mail: jeffrey.hodgson@reuters.com))</p>
